---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import youngDennis from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/dennis-hiatt-young.jpg";
import dennisToday from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/dennis-hiatt-today.jpg";
import guitarMain from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/gibson-les-paul.jpg";
import guitarDetail2 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/gibson-detail-2.jpg";
import guitarDetail3 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/gibson-detail-3.jpg";
import guitarDetail4 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/gibson-detail-4.jpg";
import poster1 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/baltimore-steam-packet-1.jpg";
import poster2 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/baltimore-steam-packet-2.jpg";
import poster3 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/baltimore-steam-packet-3.jpg";
import poster4 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/baltimore-steam-packet-4.jpg";
import poster6 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1983-gibson-les-paul-custom/baltimore-steam-packet-6.jpg";
---

<article class="dh" id="top">
  <header class="dh-hero">
    <div class="dh-hero__copy">
      <p class="dh-eyebrow">Sold · One Owner · Marin County, California</p>
      <h1>1983 Les Paul Custom:<br />Dennis Hiatt</h1>
      <p class="dh-dek">A 1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom, preserved for more than four decades and now being played and loved by its new owner.</p>
      <p class="dh-byline">The Dennis Hiatt Collection <span>·</span> Joe's Vintage Guitars</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="dh-hero__figure">
      <Image src={youngDennis} alt="Dennis Hiatt as a young musician playing his 1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom" width={1000} priority />
      <figcaption>Dennis Hiatt with his Les Paul Custom · Early 1980s</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>

  <section class="dh-story dh-intro">
    <p class="dh-dropcap">Some vintage guitars are valuable because of their rarity. Others are special because of where they have been and the music they have helped create.</p>
    <p>This one owner 1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom has both beauty and history. The ebony fingerboard, multi-ply binding, split-diamond headstock inlay, and gold hardware are Custom specifications from Gibson's Norlin era. Its story begins years before it was made.</p>
  </section>

  <figure class="dh-guitar-feature">
    <Image src={guitarMain} alt="1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom in cherry sunburst" width={1180} />
    <figcaption>1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom · Cherry Sunburst</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="dh-chapter" id="the-baltimore-steam-packet">
    <p class="dh-chapter__number">01</p>
    <div class="dh-story">
      <h2>From the Summer of Love to Capitol Records</h2>
      <p>As Dennis tells it, he joined the Baltimore Steam Packet in 1966, a Marin County rock band emerging during the height of San Francisco's psychedelic music movement.</p>
      <p>The band steadily built a following throughout the Bay Area and reached its peak during the Summer of Love in 1967. That same summer, the Baltimore Steam Packet signed a recording contract with Capitol Records and later recorded an album of original material.</p>
      <p>Dennis and the band performed throughout California, sharing stages with many of the era's leading rock groups. His instrument at the time was a 1965 Fender Jazzmaster, purchased new shortly before he joined the band.</p>
      <p>The band's manager died unexpectedly and its drummer was drafted into the Army. Without guidance, the group dissolved. Dennis moved on to college and a corporate career, then returned to playing in the late 1970s.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="dh-album-note" id="the-capitol-records-album-that-was-never-released">
    <p class="dh-eyebrow">The Lost Capitol Album</p>
    <h2>Recorded, But Never Released</h2>
    <p>The Baltimore Steam Packet completed an album of original music for Capitol Records. After the loss of their manager and the drafting of their drummer, the band came to an end. The album was shelved and never released.</p>
  </aside>

  <section class="dh-posters" aria-labelledby="dh-poster-heading">
    <div class="dh-posters__heading">
      <p class="dh-eyebrow">From the Dennis Hiatt Archive</p>
      <h2 id="dh-poster-heading">Baltimore Steam Packet Concert Posters</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="dh-poster-grid">
      <figure class="dh-poster-wide"><Image src={poster2} alt="Colorful 1967 Baltimore Steam Packet concert poster" width={760} /><figcaption>Baltimore Steam Packet · 1967</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><Image src={poster3} alt="Baltimore Steam Packet concert poster for the Ark in Phoenix" width={430} /><figcaption>Concert bill · The Ark, Phoenix</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><Image src={poster4} alt="Psychedelic dance concert poster featuring the Baltimore Steam Packet" width={430} /><figcaption>Period psychedelic concert bill</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><Image src={poster1} alt="Hand lettered Baltimore Steam Packet concert poster" width={430} /><figcaption>Vintage Baltimore Steam Packet poster</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><Image src={poster6} alt="Giant Dance concert poster featuring the Baltimore Steam Packet" width={430} /><figcaption>Giant Dance concert bill</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="dh-detail-grid" aria-label="Guitar finish and hardware details">
    <figure><Image src={guitarDetail2} alt="Close view of the Les Paul Custom cherry sunburst finish, pickups and controls" width={760} /><figcaption>Cherry sunburst · Gold hardware</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><Image src={guitarDetail3} alt="Front detail of the 1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom" width={760} /><figcaption>Carefully kept since 1983</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <blockquote>“I thought it was the nicest looking guitar I had ever seen. I bought it as soon as I saw it.”<cite>Dennis Hiatt</cite></blockquote>

  <section class="dh-chapter" id="a-return-to-playing">
    <p class="dh-chapter__number">02</p>
    <div class="dh-story">
      <h2>Love at First Sight</h2>
      <p>By the late 1970s, Dennis was playing again. A casual jam group became more than 20 years of weekend performances at parties, weddings and social events.</p>
      <p>In the early 1980s, he wanted another electric guitar to keep at home for practice. That search led him to a guitar shop in San Rafael and to a new 1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom in a striking cherry sunburst finish.</p>
      <p>Unlike many vintage instruments from working musicians, this Les Paul did not spend decades traveling from club to club. It was used primarily at home, with only occasional recording session appearances. It was never taken on the road for gigs and returned to its case whenever it was not being played.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="dh-portrait-feature" id="the-1983-les-paul-custom">
    <Image src={guitarDetail4} alt="Full length view of the 1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom" width={760} />
    <figcaption>Les Paul Custom · One Owner Provenance</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="dh-chapter">
    <p class="dh-chapter__number">03</p>
    <div class="dh-story">
      <h2>Four Decades With One Owner</h2>
      <p>Ownership history matters with any vintage guitar. Instruments pass through many hands, and the details of their early years are easily lost. There is no mystery surrounding this Les Paul.</p>
      <p>That clear history is an important part of identification and value. Owners researching a similar instrument can begin with Joe's guide to <a href="/how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/">dating a Gibson Les Paul</a>, then use the <a href="/vintage-gibson-les-paul-market-value-guide/">vintage Gibson Les Paul value guide</a> to understand how the model, year, originality and condition influence the market.</p>
      <p>It remained with the same musician from the day it was purchased new in San Rafael in 1983 until Dennis decided it was time for a new caretaker. Its history is direct, documented and inseparable from the life of its original owner.</p>
      <p>Dennis retired in 2016 and now plays only for his own enjoyment. The 1965 Jazzmaster that accompanied him through the Baltimore Steam Packet years carries too much personal history to leave him. With two electric guitars no longer necessary, the Gibson was ready to begin its next chapter.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dh-explore" aria-labelledby="dh-explore-heading">
    <div class="dh-explore__heading">
      <p class="dh-eyebrow">Explore Joe's Vintage Guitars</p>
      <h2 id="dh-explore-heading">More for Vintage Guitar Owners</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="dh-explore__links">
      <a href="/free-appraisal/"><span>01</span><strong>Get a Free Guitar Appraisal</strong><small>Learn what your vintage guitar may be worth.</small></a>
      <a href="/how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/"><span>02</span><strong>Read Gibson Serial Numbers</strong><small>Find helpful information for identifying and dating a Gibson.</small></a>
      <a href="/sell-my-gibson-guitar/"><span>03</span><strong>Sell Your Vintage Gibson</strong><small>Talk directly with Joe about your instrument and its history.</small></a>
      <a href="/blog/"><span>04</span><strong>Discover More Guitar Stories</strong><small>Meet the instruments and owners behind the history.</small></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dh-closing" id="a-new-owner-and-a-new-chapter">
    <Image class="dh-owner-today" src={dennisToday} alt="Dennis Hiatt later in life holding his one owner 1983 Gibson Les Paul Custom" width={760} />
    <p class="dh-eyebrow">Sold to Its New Owner</p>
    <h2>The Story Continues</h2>
    <p>The Les Paul Custom has found its next caretaker. It is now being played by its new owner, carrying Dennis Hiatt's story forward while beginning a new chapter of its own.</p>
    <a href="/blog/">Read More Guitar Stories</a>
  </section>
</article>

<style>
  .dh { --dh-ink:#17130f; --dh-paper:#f3eee4; --dh-wine:#6e1918; --dh-gold:#ad8146; color:var(--dh-ink); background:var(--dh-paper); overflow:hidden; }
  .dh * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  .dh-hero { min-height:860px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:46% 54%; padding-top:188px; background:#1c1713; color:#fff; }
  .dh-hero__copy { padding:clamp(60px,8vw,120px) clamp(32px,6vw,100px); display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; }
  .dh-eyebrow { font:600 11px/1.5 var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.18em; color:#bd8b4e; }
  .dh h1 { font-family:var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; font-size:clamp(56px,7.2vw,112px); line-height:.9; letter-spacing:-.025em; font-weight:600; margin:24px 0 34px; color:#fff; }
  .dh-dek { max-width:590px; font-size:clamp(21px,2vw,29px); line-height:1.38; color:#d7cbbb; margin:0; }
  .dh-byline { margin-top:44px; font:600 12px/1.5 var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.1em; color:#9f9283; }
  .dh-byline span { color:var(--dh-gold); padding:0 6px; }
  .dh figure { margin:0; position:relative; overflow:hidden; background:#3a211c; }
  .dh figure:after { content:""; position:absolute; inset:0; box-shadow:inset 30px 0 60px rgba(20,15,11,.35); pointer-events:none; }
  .dh figure :global(img) { width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block; }
  .dh-hero__figure { min-height:672px; }
  .dh-hero__figure :global(img) { object-position:center 35%; }
  .dh figcaption { position:absolute; bottom:22px; right:28px; z-index:1; font:600 10px var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.13em; color:#fff; background:rgba(20,15,12,.66); padding:10px 12px; }
  .dh-story { max-width:760px; }
  .dh-story p { font-size:20px; line-height:1.72; margin:0 0 24px; }
  .dh-story a { color:var(--dh-wine); font-weight:700; text-decoration-color:var(--dh-gold); text-decoration-thickness:2px; text-underline-offset:4px; }
  .dh-intro { margin:0 auto; padding:100px 30px 72px; }
  .dh-intro p { font-size:26px; line-height:1.55; }
  .dh-dropcap:first-letter { float:left; color:var(--dh-wine); font-size:102px; line-height:.72; padding:16px 10px 0 0; }
  .dh-guitar-feature { max-width:1180px; height:min(72vw,760px); min-height:520px; margin:0 auto 88px !important; }
  .dh-chapter { display:grid; grid-template-columns:100px minmax(0,760px); gap:44px; max-width:1050px; padding:74px 30px; margin:0 auto; border-top:1px solid #cfc4b2; }
  .dh-chapter__number { font:600 12px var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; color:var(--dh-gold); letter-spacing:.15em; margin:11px 0; }
  .dh h2 { font-family:var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,63px); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.015em; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 36px; color:var(--dh-ink); }
  .dh-album-note { max-width:980px; margin:22px auto 96px; padding:56px clamp(28px,6vw,76px); background:var(--dh-wine); color:#f7efe4; border-left:8px solid var(--dh-gold); }
  .dh-album-note .dh-eyebrow { color:#dcb98d; margin:0 0 18px; }
  .dh-album-note h2 { color:#fff; margin-bottom:24px; }
  .dh-album-note > p:last-child { max-width:760px; margin:0; font-size:20px; line-height:1.65; color:#eadfd1; }
  .dh-posters { max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto 112px; padding:0 24px; }
  .dh-posters__heading { max-width:760px; margin:0 auto 42px; text-align:center; }
  .dh-poster-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:18px; align-items:stretch; }
  .dh-poster-grid figure { min-height:390px; background:#241d18; }
  .dh-poster-grid .dh-poster-wide { grid-column:span 2; grid-row:span 2; min-height:798px; }
  .dh-poster-grid figure :global(img) { object-fit:contain; padding:14px; background:#231e1a; }
  .dh-detail-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; max-width:1180px; margin:10px auto 70px; padding:0 24px; }
  .dh-detail-grid figure { min-height:430px; }
  .dh blockquote { margin:70px 0; padding:110px max(30px,calc((100vw - 980px)/2)); background:var(--dh-wine); color:#f7efe4; text-align:center; font-size:clamp(38px,5.5vw,76px); line-height:1.05; }
  .dh blockquote cite { display:block; margin-top:30px; color:#dcb98d; font:600 11px var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.18em; }
  .dh-portrait-feature { width:min(760px,calc(100% - 48px)); height:min(125vw,980px); margin:40px auto 90px !important; }
  .dh-explore { max-width:1180px; margin:20px auto 120px; padding:76px 30px 0; border-top:1px solid #cfc4b2; }
  .dh-explore__heading { max-width:720px; margin-bottom:42px; }
  .dh-explore__links { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr); gap:16px; }
  .dh-explore__links a { min-height:190px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:46px 1fr; align-content:center; column-gap:18px; padding:30px; color:var(--dh-ink); background:#e8dfd0; border:1px solid #d0c0aa; text-decoration:none; transition:transform .2s ease,background .2s ease; }
  .dh-explore__links a:hover { transform:translateY(-3px); background:#eee6da; }
  .dh-explore__links span { grid-row:span 2; color:var(--dh-gold); font:600 12px var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; letter-spacing:.12em; }
  .dh-explore__links strong { font:600 25px/1.15 var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; }
  .dh-explore__links small { display:block; margin-top:10px; color:#62594f; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; }
  .dh-closing { margin-top:80px; padding:120px max(30px,calc((100vw - 820px)/2)); background:#211b16; color:#fff; text-align:center; }
  .dh-owner-today { width:min(100%,580px); max-height:620px; object-fit:cover; object-position:center 25%; margin:-190px auto 68px; border:10px solid var(--dh-paper); box-shadow:0 18px 50px rgba(0,0,0,.35); }
  .dh-closing h2 { color:#fff; margin:22px auto 28px; }
  .dh-closing > p:not(.dh-eyebrow) { font-size:21px; line-height:1.55; color:#cfc2b3; }
  .dh-closing > a { display:inline-block; margin-top:24px; padding:17px 28px; background:#b7864d; color:#17120e; text-decoration:none; font:600 12px var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.12em; }
  @media (max-width:900px) {
    .dh-hero { grid-template-columns:1fr; padding-top:150px; }
    .dh-hero__copy { min-height:570px; padding:70px 28px; }
    .dh-hero__figure { min-height:620px; }
    .dh-detail-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .dh-detail-grid figure { min-height:360px; }
    .dh-chapter { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:8px; padding:58px 26px; }
    .dh-story p { font-size:18px; }
    .dh-intro { padding:72px 26px 48px; }
    .dh-intro p { font-size:22px; }
    .dh-album-note { margin:10px 24px 74px; }
    .dh-poster-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }
    .dh-poster-grid .dh-poster-wide { grid-column:span 2; min-height:660px; }
    .dh-poster-grid figure { min-height:360px; }
    .dh-explore__links { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width:560px) {
    .dh-poster-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .dh-poster-grid .dh-poster-wide { grid-column:auto; grid-row:auto; min-height:520px; }
    .dh-poster-grid figure { min-height:480px; }
    .dh-explore__links a { grid-template-columns:34px 1fr; padding:24px; }
    .dh-explore__links strong { font-size:22px; }
  }
</style>
